  "canvas": { "aspect_ratio": "16:9", "background_color": "white" },
  "transcript": "Simple interest and compound interest are two ways money grows over time. With simple interest, growth is linear — each year you earn the same fixed amount on the original principal. With compound interest, growth accelerates because you earn interest on your interest as well as the principal. Over time compound interest far outpaces simple interest. The gap between them widens every year.",
